 "findings": [
  "Cgroup isolation holds on WSL 3.0.1 with two systemd distributions running: distinct cgroup namespaces, local pids only, both user managers active (run 2, probe E1, run 3).",
  "The VM console /dev/tty1 is shared: without a mask, getty@tty1.service fails with start-limit-hit in both distributions when the second one boots (run 2). The user-data bootcmd masks it before systemd starts the unit (probe E1, run 3).",
  "With the bootcmd, cloud-init records one recoverable error, 'Failed to wait for network', because WSL masks systemd-networkd-wait-online.service; result.json has no errors (run 3).",
  "Each install left one hv_storvsc driver error (cmd 0x2a, srb 0x4) inside its install window: kernel times 7118.5 s, 7678.6 s and 15573.8 s.",
  "On 3.0.1 the WSLInterop registration survived every unregister, and a file created from Windows after one terminate is owned 1000:1000.",
  "A rootless container starts in a new distribution (Docker Engine 29.8.2): microsoft/WSL issue 41492 does not affect this host.",
  "Windows PowerShell 5.1 does not escape a double quote inside an argument to a native program: two probe commands failed and were corrected (run 3, step Q-quoting)."
 ],
 "not_established": [
  "Stage 2 (the bootstrap) and its uv and Node probes; the 24.04.5 rollback arm; path B.",
  "A live workstation getty surviving a new distribution's first boot: the workstation's unit had failed in run 2 and no unit was touched.",
  "Run 3's throwaway distribution was still registered when this record was built; its removal and the interop check after it are not in this record."
 ]
